$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Mechanosynthesis of Diethyl Cyclopen-3-ene-1,1-Dicarboxylate (4b) Diethyl
diallylmalonate (4a, 484 µL, 2 mmol) was added to a 10 mL Teflon jar
charged with a single stainless steel ball bearing. A portion of catalyst
D (1.5 mg, 0.125 mol%) was added to the jar. The reaction mixture was
then milled for a period of 15 minutes. Another portion of the catalyst
was added to the reaction mixture, which was then milled for an
additional 15 minutes. The catalyst was removed from the brown colored
crude mixture, and the resulting clear, colorless to light tan liquid was
passed through a silica microcolumn, using ethyl acetate as the eluent.
The solvent is then removed by rotary evaporation. Clear, colorless to
light tan liquid (94% yield); 1H-NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 1.15 (t, J =
7.08 Hz, 6H), δ 2.89 (s, 4H), δ 4.00-4.20 (m, 4H), δ 5.59 (s, 2H) 13C-NMR
(300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 14.25, δ 40.84, δ 58.49, δ 61.63, δ 128.17, δ 171.80
HR-MS: calculated for C11H16NaO4 [M+Na] 235.0941; measured: 235.0945
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid state, incremental addition of catalyst, stainless steel ball used,
no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mechanochemical Ruthenium-Catalyzed Olefin Metathesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
