$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Mechanosynthesis of 1-((4-Nitrophenyl)Sulfonyl)-2,5-Dihydro-1H-Pyrrole
(6b) N,N-diallyl-4-nitrobenzenesulfonamide (5a, 282.3 mg,1 mmol) was
added to a 10 mL Teflon jar charged with a single stainless steel ball
bearing. 150 wt. % NaCl and a portion of catalyst D (1.0 mg, 0.167 mol%)
was added to the jar. 75 µL of ethyl acetate was used as the LAG solvent.
The reaction mixture was then milled for a period of 60 minutes. After
each milling period, another portion of the catalyst was added to the
reaction mixture and milled for another period of time for a total of 3
hours of milling time. The catalyst and salt were removed from the
grayish-brown colored crude mixture. Any remaining brown colored
residues, if any, were removed by recrystallization from hot anhydrous
ethanol, and the resulting off-white to light yellow solid was filtered
and dried in air. Off-white to light yellow powder (94% yield); 1H-NMR
(300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 4.07 (s, 4H), δ 5.73 (s, 2H), δ 8.08 (d, J = 8.82
Hz, 2H), δ 8.40 (d, J = 8.94, 2H) 13C-NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 55.39, δ
125.21, δ 125.95, δ 129.26, δ 142.26, δ 150.46 HR-MS: calculated for
C10H10N2NaO4S [M+Na] 277.0253; measured: 277.0246
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of catalyst, stainless steel ball used
