$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.5 Mechanosynthesis of Dimethyl 4,4’-Stilbenedicarboxylate (2b) Methyl
4-vinylbenzoate (2a, 324.4 mg, 2 mmol) was added to a 10 mL Teflon jar
charged with a single stainless steel ball bearing. 150 wt. % NaCl and a
portion of catalyst D (6.0 mg, 0.5 mol%) were added to the jar. The
reaction mixture was then milled for 45 minutes. Another portion of the
catalyst was added to the reaction mixture, which was then milled for an
additional 45 minutes. The catalyst and salt were removed from the purple
colored crude mixture. Any remaining purple colored residues and salt, if
any, were washed away with cold ethyl acetate and water, and the
resulting white solid was filtered and dried in air. White powder (93%
yield); 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.93 (s, 6H), δ 7.23 (s, 2H), δ 7.59
(d, J = 7.62 Hz, 4H), δ 8.05 (d, J = 7.95, 4H) 13C-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ
52.15, δ 126.60, δ 129.47, δ 130.02, δ 130.08, δ 141.16, δ 166.76 HR-MS:
calculated for C18H17O4 [M] 297.1121; measured: 297.1124
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid state, incremental addition of catalyst, optimized on catalysts and
reagents, no solvent
