$DATUM Mechanosynthesis of 1-(3,5-Dinitrobenzoyl)-2,5-Dihydro-1H-Pyrrole (5b)
N,N-diallyl-3,5-dinitrobenzamide (6a, 291.26 mg, 1 mmol) was added to a
10 mL Teflon jar charged with a single stainless steel ball bearing. 150
wt. % NaCl and a portion of catalyst D (1.0 mg, 0.167 mol%) was added to
the jar. 75 µL of ethyl acetate was used as the LAG solvent. The reaction
mixture was then milled for a period of 60 minutes. After each milling
period, another portion of the catalyst was added to the reaction mixture
and milled for another period of time for a total of 3 hours of milling
time. The catalyst and salt were removed from the beige-brown colored
crude mixture. Any remaining brown colored residues, if any, were removed
by recrystallization from hot anhydrous ethanol, and the resulting
off-white to light yellow solid was filtered and dried in air. Off-white
to light yellow powder (92% yield); 1H-NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 4.22 (s,
2H), δ 4.32 (s, 2H), δ 5.82-5.88 (m, 1H), δ 5.93-5.99 (m, 1H), δ
8.74-8.77 (d, J = 2.13, 2H), δ 8.55-8.89 (t, J = 2.04, 1H) 13C-NMR (300
MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 53.96, δ 55.57, δ 119.92, δ 125.74, δ 126.31, δ 127.95, δ
139.96, δ 148.54, δ 164.66 HR-MS: calculated for C11H9N3NaO5 [M+Na]:
286.0443; measured: 286.0434
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of catalyst, stainless steel ball used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
