$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 15-(Tert-butyl) 14a-ethyl
(2R,6S,13aS,14aR,16aS,Z)-6-((tert-butoxycarbonyl)amino)-2-((3-chloro-7-methoxyquinoxalin-2-yl)oxy)-5,16-dioxo-2,3,6,7,8,9,10,11,13a,14,16,16a-dodecahydrocyclopropa[e]pyrrolo[1,2-a][1,4]
diazacyclopentadecine-14a,15(1H,5H)-dicarboxylate (2). To a 2 L flask was
charged compound 16 (44.2 g, 54 mmol) and toluene (800 mL) and the
mixture bubbled subsurface with N2 for 30 min. The solution was then
heated to 80°C, and a solution of Zhan-1B catalyst (0.17 g, 0.23 mmol) in
toluene (100 mL) was added to the flask over 30 min. The reaction was
aged at 80 °C for 1 h whereby HPLC analysis indicated full conversion of
16 had °Ccurred. The reaction mixture was cooled down to 50°C,
2-mercaptonicotinic acid (0.72 g, 4.6 mmol) was added and the reaction
mixture was aged at 50 °C for 1 h. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt,
and washed with 5% NaHCO3 twice and brine once. The organic layer was
concentrated down, then crystallized from IPAc/heptane (1:4). 2 (39.15 g)
as a white solid with 96.7% LCAP, 99% wt in 91% corrected yield. 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.24 (t, J = 7.12 Hz, 3 H), 1.32 (m, 11 H), 1.46 (m,
3 H), 1.51 (s, 9 H), 1.58-1.63 (m, 1 H), 1.73-1.67 (m, 1 H), 1.90-1.86
(m, 2 H), 2.15 (d, J = 8.41 Hz, 2 H), 2.60-2.48 (m, 2 H), 2.93 (t, J =
10.91 Hz, 1 H), 3.97 (s, 3 H), 4.23-4.10 (m, 3 H), 4.39 (t, J = 10.81 Hz,
2 H), 5.14 (d, J = 8.31 Hz, 1 H), 5.44 (t, J = 10.10 Hz, 1 H), 5.59-5.53
(m, 2 H), 5.83 (s, 1 H), 7.18 (d, J = 2.76 Hz, 1 H), 7.82 (d, J = 9.10
Hz, 1 H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 14.3, 21.3, 26.0, 26.6, 27.2, 28.0,
28.2, 30.8, 31.3, 35.2, 45.0, 51.3, 53.1, 55.8, 61.0, 61.3, 75.9, 79.6,
83.7, 105.9, 119.8, 124.8, 128.8, 133.7, 134.0, 136.2, 141.0, 152.3,
152.5, 161.2, 170.0, 171.6, 177.5; HRMS (ESI) calculated for
C39H53ClN5O10 + (M+H): 786.3481. Found: 786.3469.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM cross-metathesis
